            <ArticleTitle>[Practical problems in the long-term drug treatment of ischemic heart disease and hypertension].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>162-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In choosing drugs for treatment of ischemic heart disease or hypertension one has--next to effects on angina or blood pressure--to consider possible influences on long term course. A simple dosing-scheme with a low number of tablets as well as a thorough information of the patient about the prescribed medication are equally important for the therapeutic success.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
